{
  "_comment": "POMS (Profile of Mood States) catalog onboarding. Source: McNair, D. M., Lorr, M., & Droppleman, L. F. (1971). Manual for the Profile of Mood States. San Diego, CA: Educational and Industrial Testing Service. Original 65-item, 6-factor instrument; 58 of the 65 items are scored into the six factors below (Tension-Anxiety 9, Depression-Dejection 15, Anger-Hostility 12, Vigor-Activity 8, Fatigue-Inertia 7, Confusion-Bewilderment 7 = 58), the remaining 7 items are unscored filler/buffer adjectives with no factor assignment -- they are intentionally NOT registered here, since the GDX_PSY schema requires every catalogued item to feed a variable, and inventing a placeholder construct for literally-unscored filler words would misrepresent the instrument. Item wording and factor/reverse-scoring assignment were read directly from an independent scale-scoring reference (brianmac.co.uk coaching-science resource) that reproduces the official McNair et al. scoring key; the resulting item counts (9/15/12/8/7/7=58, +7 unscored) match the widely documented POMS factor structure. Within-factor item ORDER here is grouped by factor for catalog clarity; the original manual interleaves items from different factors in a fixed non-grouped sequence, but that exact published order could not be independently verified from open sources, so grouped-by-factor order is used instead (sum-based factor scoring is unaffected by item presentation order). Response scale (0 Not at all .. 4 Extremely) and the two reverse-scored items (Relaxed within Tension-Anxiety, Efficient within Confusion-Bewilderment) are well-documented and cross-confirmed. The instrument also yields a well-known derived Total Mood Disturbance (TMD) score (sum of the five negative factors minus Vigor-Activity, plus a constant); TMD is NOT modelled as a separate GDX_PSY_CONSTRUCT here because it is a cross-indicator composite with no schema mechanism to compute an indicator from other indicators (the same modelling choice already made for SEES's three independent subscales) -- it is documented here for context only.",
  "study": {
    "study_type": "PSYCHOMETRIC",
    "title": "Profile of Mood States (POMS) - Instrument Onboarding",
    "objective": "Register the POMS instrument and its six mood-state dimensions into the GDX_HUMAN psychometric catalog as reusable knowledge for future mood/affect studies.",
    "method": "Desk research of the published instrument (McNair, Lorr & Droppleman, 1971) and an independent scoring-key reference; catalog registration only, no primary data collection associated with this record.",
    "start_date": "2026-10-17",
    "end_date": null,
    "status": "PLANNED"
  },
  "instruments": [
